Explanation: In the Remove method, the method checks if the element exists in the list and if it does, it calls the RemoveAt method to remove the element at the specified index. In the RemoveAt method, the element at the specified index is removed from the list. To ensure that the array does not contain any references to the removed element, the old element value is compared with the old value of array at index and is compared with the new value using the != (not equal) operator. Hence the assert statement checks that the old element value (value of _items[index]) in the array is not equal to the new value (value of value).
